Specify the exact location(s) where the Great Lakes meet the Atlantic Ocean, including any notable geographical features or landmarks
Based on the provided context, the Great Lakes meet the Atlantic Ocean through the Saint Lawrence River. Specifically, the Saint Lawrence River connects the Great Lakes to the Atlantic Ocean, and the Gulf of Saint Lawrence is the outlet of the North American Great Lakes via the Saint Lawrence River into the Atlantic Ocean.

Notable geographical features or landmarks in this area include:

* The Labrador Peninsula and Quebec to the north
* Saint-Pierre and Newfoundland to the east
* The Nova Scotia peninsula and Cape Breton Island to the south
* The Gaspe Peninsula, New Brunswick to the west

These geographical features bound the Gulf of Saint Lawrence, which is the location where the Great Lakes meet the Atlantic Ocean.
