The first successful launch of a manmade object into space was Sputnik 1, launched by the Soviet Union on October 4, 1957. Sputnik 1 was a small, beach-ball-sized satellite that weighed about 83 kg (184 lbs) and measured 58 cm (23 inches) in diameter. It was equipped with a radio transmitter that broadcast a beep-tone signal, allowing scientists to track its movement and altitude. Sputnik 1 reached an altitude of about 225 km (140 miles) and completed 1,440 orbits around the Earth before burning up in the atmosphere on January 4, 1958.
