Michael Jordan's last basketball games before his initial retirement were in the 1993-1994 NBA season. He announced his retirement on October 6, 1993, citing a loss of desire to play the game, which was also influenced by the death of his father, James R. Jordan, Sr., who was murdered on July 23, 1993.
