* 1845: Kamehameha III moved the permanent capital of the Hawaiian Kingdom from Lahaina on Maui to Honolulu.
* 1850: Kamehameha III declared Honolulu to be the official capital of the Kingdom of Hawaiʻi.

Therefore, Honolulu became the capital of Hawaii in 1845.
